 "name": "Burg Hohenzollern",
 "building": "architecture/hohenzollern",
 "_about": "Burg Hohenzollern: the walls of the castle and its bastions in the hill's own Jurassic limestone and sandstone, a muted buff-grey ashlar (warmer than the 'grey-white' it is often called; the photographs show buff and ochre), the window surrounds and the chapels' dressings a shade darker; dark blue-grey slate on every roof, cone and spire; the Michaelsturm's cap and the fl\u00e8che's lead; St Michael's chapel plastered white; the courts and the road in gravel and setts, the summit's slopes grass. Inside: plastered walls, the Grafensaal's vaults ochre on grey marble columns, marble floors in the state rooms, flagstones in the chapels.",
